  "name": "@idrivee2/s3-mcp",
  "readme": "# @idrivee2/s3-mcp\n\nA local Model Context Protocol (MCP) server for managing IDrive e2\nS3-compatible object storage. It provides an authenticated Streamable HTTP MCP\nendpoint with tools for regions, buckets, objects, multipart uploads, and\npresigned URLs.\n\n## Requirements\n\n- Node.js 20 or newer\n- An IDrive e2 account\n\n## Install\n\nInstall globally to use the command from any terminal:\n\n```sh\nnpm install --global @idrivee2/s3-mcp\n```\n\nOr install it in a Node.js project:\n\n```sh\nnpm install @idrivee2/s3-mcp\n```\n\n## Run\n\nAfter installation:\n\n```sh\nidrivee2-s3-mcp\n```\n\nThe server starts in the background and prints its process ID, MCP URL, and log\nfile. The default MCP URL is:\n\n```text\nhttp://127.0.0.1:1908/s3\n```\n\nAdd this URL to an MCP client that supports Streamable HTTP and OAuth. The client\nwill open the local IDrive e2 sign-in page when authentication is required.\n\n## Server commands\n\n```sh\nidrivee2-s3-mcp --status\nidrivee2-s3-mcp --stop\nidrivee2-s3-mcp --foreground\nidrivee2-s3-mcp --foreground --debug\n```\n\n## Parameters\n\n| Parameter            | Description                                          |\n| -------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------- |\n| `--web-port <port>`  | Login and OAuth port. Default: `1907`                |\n| `--mcp-port <port>`  | MCP server port. Default: `1908`                     |\n| `--host <host>`      | Address used by both listeners. Default: `127.0.0.1` |\n| `--public-url <url>` | Public HTTPS origin when using a reverse proxy       |\n| `--data-dir <path>`  | Directory for encrypted local state                  |\n| `--cleanup`          | Delete encrypted local state and start fresh         |\n| `--foreground`       | Keep the server attached to the terminal             |\n| `--status`           | Show the background server status                    |\n| `--stop`             | Stop the background server                           |\n| `--debug`            | Enable diagnostic logging                            |\n| `-h`, `--help`       | Show command help                                    |\n| `-v`, `--version`    | Show the package version                             |\n\nCommand-line parameters override environment variables.\n\n## IDrive e2 resources\n\n- [Website](https://www.idrive.com/s3-storage-e2/)\n- [FAQ](https://www.idrive.com/s3-storage-e2/faq)\n- [Support](https://www.idrive.com/s3-storage-e2/support)\n- [Sign in to IDrive e2](https://console.idrivee2.com/)\n\n## License\n\nUNLICENSED\n",
  "readmeFilename": "README.md",
